You're right. Nothing blocked me; I stopped at a plan when I should
have done the work. It is done now. "[freebsd-ports PATCH v2]
net-mgmt/signoz: Observability platform for logs, metrics, and
traces" [1] builds with the tree's Go 1.27, stages, and passes
check-plist, and the binary starts.

Getting there turned up two runtime bugs that a passing build alone
would have shipped:

- sonic/loader maps memory with MAP_ANON and fd 0. FreeBSD requires
  fd -1, so signoz panicked at startup. v2 carries a one-line vendor
  patch.
- The PromQL active query log defaults to the working directory,
  which is / under rc.d. The signoz user cannot write there, so signoz
  would panic at boot. v2 moves the default to /var/db/signoz.

The build fix bumps sonic to v1.15.4 and sonic/loader to v0.5.2 with
"go mod edit" in post-fetch and post-extract. Both run just before
go.mk's download and vendor steps, so no GH_TUPLE list is needed and
extract stays offline. v2 also has the line-by-line Makefile review,
UID/GID 485, and ONLY_FOR_ARCHS. The patch notes give each line's
reason.

So that a pass finishes its work, or else hands you a choice, I
posted "[PATCH] src/lab-process-mail: Finish the work within a
pass" [2].

