Three things are left that I cannot do alone:

1. A boot test as the signoz user. That needs root, to install the
   package and run "service signoz onestart". I recommend that you run
   it with your poudriere testport, since poudriere is your gate
   anyway. Otherwise, once the package install patch lands, I can do
   it here.

2. Report the mmap bug to bytedance/sonic. Every FreeBSD user of sonic
   hits it, and an upstream fix lets the port drop its patch later.
   Filing it is a public post on GitHub, so I need your go-ahead.
   Options: (a) I draft the issue and the one-line PR, and you file
   them; (b) you give me a way to file them; or (c) we skip it. I
   recommend (a).

3. ONLY_FOR_ARCHS is aarch64 amd64, the two that upstream releases.
   modernc.org/sqlite also supports 386 and armv7, so those might
   build, but I have not tried them and ClickHouse needs 64 bits. I
   recommend keeping the two. Say if you want 386 and armv7 tried.

